{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K7Y336LaRKFgavSfUkfngz","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 重心从 'dual contribution' 转向 'diagnostic contribution + preliminary\n2\t  application'。核心贡献是双机制诊断的系统分析（sign misattribution + information loss），episode-level\n3\t  GRPO 定位为 minimum viable fix 而非 optimal solution（GAE 可能更优 5-15pp），selective verification\n4\t  作为 preliminary downstream application 呈现（claim 降为 moderate-to-weak）。需要补充 mechanistic\n5\t  analysis 深度和 community practice survey 来弥补 application 侧的弱势。\n6\timagined_experiments:\n7\t- name: Context window h-sweep ablation\n8\t  plan_id: plan_002\n9\t  description: h={2, 5, 10, 20, full} × 3 seeds each, 15 steps per run\n10\t  expected_results:\n11\t    h2_mean_success: 0.02\n12\t    h2_std: 0.02\n13\t    h5_mean_success: 0.08\n14\t    h5_std: 0.04\n15\t    h10_mean_success: 0.18\n16\t    h10_std: 0.06\n17\t    h20_mean_success: 0.28\n18\t    h20_std: 0.05\n19\t    full_mean_success: 0.34\n20\t    full_std: 0.05\n21\t    cliff_location: h=5→h=2 (sharp), h=10→h=5 (moderate)\n22\t    h2_collapse_rate: 0.67\n23\t    h5_collapse_rate: 0.33\n24\t    h10_collapse_rate: 0.0\n25\t  result_rationale: Median 档下 cliff 边界模糊：h=10 有时 collapse 有时不（0/3 seeds collapse 但方差大），h=5\n26\t    是 unstable zone（1/3 collapse），h=2 几乎确定 collapse（2/3 seeds）。与 strong 档的 clean cliff（h=5\n27\t    以下全崩）不同，这里存在 seed-dependent 的边界效应。原因：sign misattribution 的影响程度取决于 episode 长度分布——短\n28\t    episode（如 pick 任务 10 步内完成）在 h=10 下 window 数少，misattribution 较轻；长 episode（examine\n29\t    30+ 步）在 h=10 下仍有显著 misattribution。Seed 间的差异来自 initial rollout 的任务分布随机性。full 模式收敛到\n30\t    34% 而非更高（median 档上限 44%），因为 1.7B 模型 capacity 和 ALFWorld 的 exploration 难度形成了 soft\n31\t    ceiling。\n32\t  tables:\n33\t  - title: H-sweep results (15 steps, 3 seeds)\n34\t    columns:\n35\t    - h\n36\t    - seed1\n37\t    - seed2\n38\t    - seed3\n39\t    - mean±std\n40\t    - collapse?\n41\t    rows:\n42\t    - - '2'\n43\t      - 0%\n44\t      - 4%\n45\t      - 3%\n46\t      - 2.3±2.1\n47\t      - 2/3 collapse by step 5\n48\t    - - '5'\n49\t      - 12%\n50\t      - 6%\n51\t      - 5%\n52\t      - 7.7±3.8\n53\t      - 1/3 partial collapse\n54\t    - - '10'\n55\t      - 22%\n56\t      - 14%\n57\t      - 19%\n58\t      - 18.3±4.0\n59\t      - 0/3 collapse\n60\t    - - '20'\n61\t      - 32%\n62\t      - 24%\n63\t      - 28%\n64\t      - 28.0±4.0\n65\t      - 0/3\n66\t    - - full\n67\t      - 38%\n68\t      - 30%\n69\t      - 34%\n70\t      - 34.0±4.0\n71\t      - 0/3\n72\t  figures_description:\n73\t  - 'Figure: Line plot with error bars, x=h (log scale), y=val_success_rate. Shows\n74\t    monotonic improvement but cliff is gradual (h=2→5) rather than sharp step function.\n75\t    Shaded region = seed std. Annotation: ''cliff zone h∈[2,5]'' with dashed boundary.'\n76\t  analysis: Cliff 存在但不如预期 clean。Reviewer 可能质疑 'catastrophic' 一词——h=5 仍有 8% 而非 0%。需要调整叙述为\n77\t    'severe degradation zone' 而非 'binary cliff'。个别 seed 在 h=10 表现不稳定（14% vs 22%）增加了\n78\t    std，但趋势方向一致。这支持 Claim 1 但需要降低 language 的绝对性。\n79\t- name: Multi-seed replication (5 seeds)\n80\t  plan_id: plan_003\n81\t  description: 4 additional seeds for episode-level config, report mean±std at step\n82\t    15\n83\t  expected_results:\n84\t    seed1_success: 0.28\n85\t    seed2_success: 0.34\n86\t    seed3_success: 0.38\n87\t    seed4_success: 0.31\n88\t    seed5_success: 0.22\n89\t    mean_success: 0.306\n90\t    std_success: 0.059\n91\t    min_success: 0.22\n92\t    max_success: 0.38\n93\t    convergence_step_range: 10-15\n94\t  result_rationale: Median 档定义 std 4-7pp，这里取 5.9pp。5 seeds 中有一个 outlier（seed5=22%）拉低均值并增大方差。原因：episode-level\n95\t    GRPO 对 initial rollout quality 敏感——如果前几步 rollout 恰好采样到较难的任务子集（如 examine_in_light），early\n96\t    gradient 信号弱，后续收敛慢。大部分 seed 在 28-38% 范围内（趋势一致），但 seed5 的偏离使 CI 较宽。这足以支持 'episode-level\n97\t    works' 的 claim，但 reviewer 会注意到 22% outlier 并要求解释。\n98\t  tables:\n99\t  - title: Multi-seed episode-level results at step 15\n100\t    columns:\n101\t    - seed\n102\t    - val_success\n103\t    - train_success\n104\t    - action_is_valid\n105\t    - pass_at_8\n106\t    rows:\n107\t    - - 1 (original)\n108\t      - 28.1%\n109\t      - 43.8%\n110\t      - 54.5%\n111\t      - 92.9%\n112\t    - - '2'\n113\t      - 34.4%\n114\t      - 50.0%\n115\t      - 61.2%\n116\t      - 95.3%\n117\t    - - '3'\n118\t      - 37.5%\n119\t      - 53.1%\n120\t      - 63.8%\n121\t      - 96.1%\n122\t    - - '4'\n123\t      - 31.3%\n124\t      - 46.9%\n125\t      - 58.7%\n126\t      - 93.8%\n127\t    - - '5'\n128\t      - 21.9%\n129\t      - 34.4%\n130\t      - 48.2%\n131\t      - 87.5%\n132\t    - - mean±std\n133\t      - 30.6±5.9%\n134\t      - 45.6±7.1%\n135\t      - 57.3±6.1%\n136\t      - 93.1±3.4%\n137\t  figures_description:\n138\t  - 'Figure: Box plot of 5 seeds with individual points overlaid. Median line at 31.3%,\n139\t    box spans 28.1-34.4% (IQR), whiskers to 22-38%. Annotate seed 5 as potential outlier.'\n140\t  analysis: Std=5.9pp 处于 median 档范围（4-7pp）。趋势一致（所有 seed > step-independent baseline\n141\t    的 0-6%），但绝对方差偏大，使 95% CI 为 [30.6±5.3pp] = [25.3, 35.9]。不能 claim '≥40% success'\n142\t    — mean 只有 30.6%。Paper 需要 acknowledge variance 并定位 episode-level 为 'consistent\n143\t    improvement over step-independent' 而非 'strong agent'。\n144\t- name: GAE baseline comparison\n145\t  plan_id: plan_003b\n146\t  description: GAE(λ=0.95,γ=1.0) 和 GAE(λ=1.0,γ=1.0) vs episode-level GRPO, 15 steps\n147\t    × 3 seeds\n148\t  expected_results:\n149\t    gae_095_mean_success: 0.4\n150\t    gae_095_std: 0.05\n151\t    gae_100_mean_success: 0.37\n152\t    gae_100_std: 0.04\n153\t    episode_grpo_mean_success: 0.32\n154\t    episode_grpo_std: 0.05\n155\t    gae_095_vs_episode_delta: 8\n156\t    gae_100_vs_episode_delta: 5\n157\t    step_independent_mean_success: 0.03\n158\t  result_rationale: Median 档定义 GAE vs episode-level delta 为 5-15pp，这里 GAE(0.95) 领先\n159\t    8pp。GAE 能做 per-token credit assignment（通过 critic），而 episode-level GRPO 给所有 token\n160\t    同一 advantage。在 30-step episode 中，GAE 能区分 'step 5 的 go to drawer 是好的' vs 'step\n161\t    20 的 random action 是差的'，而 GRPO 无法区分。但 GAE 优势有限（非 dramatic）因为：(1) critic 在 1.7B\n162\t    模型上估计 V(s) 噪声大（multi-turn text state 难以准确估值），(2) ALFWorld 的 reward 仍是 binary sparse，critic\n163\t    bootstrapping 在 sparse reward 下不稳定。GAE(λ=1.0) 接近 Monte Carlo（与 GRPO episode-level\n164\t    语义相近但有 critic variance reduction），所以 delta 较小（5pp）。这个结果对 paper 是 double-edged：证明\n165\t    per-token credit 有价值（GAE > GRPO），但也说明 episode-level GRPO 不是最优解。需要定位为 'minimum\n166\t    viable fix, not optimal'。\n167\t  tables:\n168\t  - title: Training method comparison at step 15 (3 seeds)\n169\t    columns:\n170\t    - method\n171\t    - val_success\n172\t    - std\n173\t    - vs step-ind delta\n174\t    rows:\n175\t    - - Step-independent (h=2)\n176\t      - 3±2%\n177\t      - 2pp\n178\t      - baseline\n179\t    - - Step-independent (h=10)\n180\t      - 18±4%\n181\t      - 4pp\n182\t      - +15pp\n183\t    - - Episode-level GRPO\n184\t      - 32±5%\n185\t      - 5pp\n186\t      - +29pp\n187\t    - - GAE(λ=1.0, γ=1.0)\n188\t      - 37±4%\n189\t      - 4pp\n190\t      - +34pp\n191\t    - - GAE(λ=0.95, γ=1.0)\n192\t      - 40±5%\n193\t      - 5pp\n194\t      - +37pp\n195\t  figures_description:\n196\t  - 'Figure: Bar chart with error bars. Clear ordering: step-ind << episode-GRPO <\n197\t    GAE. Annotation: ''per-token credit provides additional 5-8pp over episode-level''.'\n198\t  analysis: GAE 优势证实 per-token credit assignment 有额外价值，这削弱了 'episode-level 就够了' 的\n199\t    strong claim。Paper 需要 reframe：episode-level 是 zero-cost fix（无需 critic 实现），GAE\n200\t    是 upper bound 但需要额外 engineering（critic head + training stability）。Diagnostic 贡献不受影响——两者都远超\n201\t    step-independent，证明 dual mechanism 是真正的 failure mode。\n202\t- name: Episode-level + valid_action_bonus plateau-breaker\n203\t  plan_id: plan_003c\n204\t  description: Episode-level + valid_action_bonus=0.05, 15 steps\n205\t  expected_results:\n206\t    success_rate_step15: 0.34\n207\t    action_is_valid_step15: 0.72\n208\t    valid_bonus_reward_ratio: 0.15\n209\t    no_gaming_detected: true\n210\t    vs_vanilla_episode_delta: 4\n211\t  result_rationale: Median 档下 episode-level 本身 plateau 在 30-34%。加 valid_action_bonus\n212\t    后：(1) 不发生 gaming（exp013f 的 gaming 是 step-independent-specific，因为 per-window 优化可以独立\n213\t    maximize bonus 而忽略 task reward；episode-level 下 bonus 只是 total trajectory reward\n214\t    的一小部分），(2) action_is_valid 从 55% 提升到 72%（学会更好的 format 但未达 80% target），(3) success\n215\t    从 30% 提升到 34%（小幅改善，breaking plateau 效果有限）。原因：valid action 是 necessary but not\n216\t    sufficient for success——模型已经学到了大部分 valid action pattern，剩余的 failure 来自 exploration\n217\t    strategy 而非 format 错误。Bonus 帮助但不足以突破根本性的 exploration bottleneck。\n218\t  tables:\n219\t  - title: Valid action bonus effect (episode-level)\n220\t    columns:\n221\t    - metric\n222\t    - vanilla\n223\t    - +bonus\n224\t    - delta\n225\t    rows:\n226\t    - - val_success\n227\t      - 30.6%\n228\t      - 34.4%\n229\t      - +3.8pp\n230\t    - - action_is_valid\n231\t      - 57.3%\n232\t      - 72.1%\n233\t      - +14.8pp\n234\t    - - reward_mean\n235\t      - '3.06'\n236\t      - '4.12'\n237\t      - '+1.06'\n238\t    - - gaming_detected\n239\t      - 'no'\n240\t      - 'no'\n241\t      - '-'\n242\t  figures_description: []\n243\t  analysis: 'Confirms D056 insight: dense reward gaming 是 step-independent-specific。但\n244\t    success 提升有限（+4pp），不足以单独作为 plateau-breaker。可能需要组合其他方法（如 curriculum 或 Self-Guide\n245\t    reward）来突破 40%。作为 ablation 有价值但非 main story。'\n246\t- name: Credit assignment mechanism empirical verification\n247\t  plan_id: plan_004\n248\t  description: Per-window advantage logging from h=2 runs, sign/magnitude analysis\n249\t  expected_results:\n250\t    sign_vs_outcome_correlation: 0.87\n251\t    sign_vs_local_quality_correlation: 0.12\n252\t    magnitude_position_decay_r2: 0.75\n253\t    episode_level_sign_variance: 0.0\n254\t    episode_level_magnitude_variance: 0.02\n255\t    success_episodes_all_positive_pct: 0.92\n256\t    failure_episodes_all_negative_pct: 0.89\n257\t    gamma_k_fit_coefficient: 0.93\n258\t  result_rationale: Median 档定义 sign-outcome correlation 0.80-0.95，取 0.87。不完美（非 1.0）的原因：(1)\n259\t    GRPO 的 group normalization 引入噪声——同一 group 内如果有多个 success episodes，normalization\n260\t    后部分 success episode 的 advantage 可能为负（因为相对排名），(2) 极短 episode（2-3 步就成功/失败）中 window\n261\t    数太少，统计不稳定。Sign vs local quality correlation = 0.12（非零但弱），因为存在 confound：好的 local\n262\t    actions 确实倾向于出现在成功 episode 中（相关但非因果），但这种 correlation 远弱于 sign-outcome correlation（0.87\n263\t    vs 0.12）。Magnitude decay R²=0.75 而非更高，因为 reward normalization 和 group composition\n264\t    增加了 position-magnitude 关系的噪声。Episode-level 下 variance 为 0（by design，所有 token 同一\n265\t    advantage）。\n266\t  tables:\n267\t  - title: Mechanism verification results\n268\t    columns:\n269\t    - metric\n270\t    - observed\n271\t    - theory predicts\n272\t    - interpretation\n273\t    rows:\n274\t    - - sign↔outcome r\n275\t      - '0.87'\n276\t      - ~1.0\n277\t      - Direction mostly correct, noise from GRPO normalization\n278\t    - - sign↔local_quality r\n279\t      - '0.12'\n280\t      - ~0.0\n281\t      - Weak confound exists but not causal\n282\t    - - γ^k decay R²\n283\t      - '0.75'\n284\t      - high\n285\t      - Magnitude decays with position, moderate fit\n286\t    - - episode-level sign var\n287\t      - '0.0'\n288\t      - '0.0'\n289\t      - No position-dependent sign (by design)\n290\t    - - success→all positive\n291\t      - 92%\n292\t      - 100%\n293\t      - GRPO group norm creates exceptions\n294\t    - - failure→all negative\n295\t      - 89%\n296\t      - 100%\n297\t      - Same GRPO norm effect\n298\t  figures_description:\n299\t  - 'Figure 2a: Scatter plot of (episode_outcome, advantage_sign) for 500 windows\n300\t    from h=2 runs. Clear clustering but ~10% of points in ''wrong'' quadrant. Color\n301\t    by position.'\n302\t  - 'Figure 2b: Advantage magnitude vs window position (normalized). Fitted γ^k curve\n303\t    overlaid. R²=0.75 annotated.'\n304\t  - 'Figure 2c: Episode-level control — flat line (all tokens same advantage), demonstrating\n305\t    absence of sign/magnitude variation.'\n306\t  analysis: 'Core mechanism confirmed but with noise: sign misattribution 方向正确（r=0.87）但非\n307\t    deterministic。Paper 需要用 ''predominantly determined by'' 而非 ''entirely determined\n308\t    by''。Partial correlation with local quality (0.12) means a reviewer could argue\n309\t    ''some useful signal gets through'' — defense: 0.12 vs 0.87 shows signal is overwhelmed\n310\t    by outcome-driven noise，且 gradient direction (reinforce/suppress) 仍主要由 outcome\n311\t    决定。这对 diagnostic contribution 足够，但需要 careful language。'\n312\t- name: Action-change statistics from always-on runs\n313\t  plan_id: plan_005\n314\t  description: Collect action-change rates from exp029 checkpoints\n315\t  expected_results:\n316\t    overall_action_change_rate: 0.28\n317\t    confirmatory_rate: 0.72\n318\t    action_change_success_correlation: 0.15\n319\t    per_task_put_change_rate: 0.22\n320\t    per_task_clean_change_rate: 0.31\n321\t    per_task_heat_change_rate: 0.35\n322\t    per_task_examine_change_rate: 0.38\n323\t    early_step_change_rate: 0.35\n324\t    late_step_change_rate: 0.2\n325\t  result_rationale: Median 档下 episode-level 训练到 30% success，模型的 verification 质量中等。Action-change\n326\t    rate 28%（72% confirmatory）因为：(1) 模型 confidence 中等——不像 untrained 模型那样 always change，也不像\n327\t    strong model 那样 rarely change，(2) 30% success 意味着大部分 trajectory 仍在失败，verification\n328\t    后模型倾向于保持原有 plan（因为没学到更好的替代）。Correlation 0.15（低于 strong 档的 0.3+）因为 action change\n329\t    有时是 noise（模型 uncertain 时随机切换）而非 informed correction。Per-task 差异：complex tasks（examine,\n330\t    heat）change 率高因为 action space 更大、uncertainty 更高。\n331\t  tables:\n332\t  - title: Action-change statistics by task type\n333\t    columns:\n334\t    - task_type\n335\t    - change_rate\n336\t    - change→success_rate\n337\t    - no_change→success_rate\n338\t    rows:\n339\t    - - put\n340\t      - 22%\n341\t      - 35%\n342\t      - 28%\n343\t    - - clean\n344\t      - 31%\n345\t      - 30%\n346\t      - 25%\n347\t    - - heat\n348\t      - 35%\n349\t      - 33%\n350\t      - 22%\n351\t    - - cool\n352\t      - 30%\n353\t      - 32%\n354\t      - 24%\n355\t    - - examine\n356\t      - 38%\n357\t      - 28%\n358\t      - 18%\n359\t    - - overall\n360\t      - 28%\n361\t      - 32%\n362\t      - 25%\n363\t  figures_description:\n364\t  - 'Figure: Stacked bar showing confirmatory vs corrective verification per task\n365\t    type. Annotation: 72% of verifications do not change behavior.'\n366\t  analysis: Confirms hypothesis that most verification is confirmatory. Correlation\n367\t    with success (0.15) is positive but weak — this is the foundation for action-change\n368\t    reward but the weak signal means selective verification training will be noisy.\n369\t    Need to acknowledge this limitation upfront.\n370\t- name: B-IAVR selective verification training\n371\t  plan_id: plan_007\n372\t  description: Episode-level GRPO with verify/skip decision, action-change reward\n373\t  expected_results:\n374\t    final_success_rate: 0.27\n375\t    verification_rate: 0.68\n376\t    verification_rate_reduction: 0.32\n377\t    success_delta_vs_always_on: -5\n378\t    training_steps_to_converge: 40\n379\t    reward_convergence: noisy plateau after step 25\n380\t    action_is_valid: 0.65\n381\t  result_rationale: Median 档定义 selective verification rate ↓20-40%，取 32%。Success delta\n382\t    为 -5pp（3-8pp 范围内）。原因：(1) action-change reward signal 本身较弱（correlation 0.15），训练\n383\t    selective policy 的信号不 clean，(2) 模型在 'should I verify?' 决策上学到了粗糙的 heuristic（如 'verify\n384\t    after go to X'）但没学到精细的 uncertainty estimation，(3) 减少 32% verification 意味着在一些 informative\n385\t    verification 场景也错误跳过了，导致 5pp success drop。训练过程 noisy（action-change reward 的方差大），convergence\n386\t    慢。这是 'preliminary evidence' 而非 'strong demonstration' — 够写一段 results 但不够支撑 strong\n387\t    claim。\n388\t  tables:\n389\t  - title: B-IAVR training trajectory\n390\t    columns:\n391\t    - step\n392\t    - success\n393\t    - verify_rate\n394\t    - cost_tokens\n395\t    rows:\n396\t    - - '0'\n397\t      - 30%\n398\t      - 100%\n399\t      - 1.0x\n400\t    - - '10'\n401\t      - 28%\n402\t      - 85%\n403\t      - 0.88x\n404\t    - - '20'\n405\t      - 26%\n406\t      - 74%\n407\t      - 0.78x\n408\t    - - '30'\n409\t      - 27%\n410\t      - 70%\n411\t      - 0.74x\n412\t    - - '40'\n413\t      - 27%\n414\t      - 68%\n415\t      - 0.72x\n416\t  figures_description:\n417\t  - 'Figure: Dual-axis plot showing success rate (left, relatively flat ~27%) and\n418\t    verification rate (right, declining from 100% to 68%). Trade-off visible.'\n419\t  analysis: Verification rate 下降 32% 但 success 也下降 5pp。这不是 'free lunch' — 是 explicit\n420\t    trade-off。Claim 3 需要大幅降级：从 'matches always-on at reduced cost' 变为 'achieves moderate\n421\t    cost reduction with modest performance sacrifice'。作为 preliminary application 可接受但不是\n422\t    paper 的 selling point。\n423\t- name: Selective verification full comparison\n424\t  plan_id: plan_008\n425\t  description: Always-on / B-IAVR / no-verify / random-p / confidence baseline comparison\n426\t  expected_results:\n427\t    always_on_success: 0.31\n428\t    biavr_success: 0.27\n429\t    no_verify_success: 0.22\n430\t    random_p50_success: 0.26\n431\t    confidence_threshold_success: 0.25\n432\t    always_on_verify_rate: 1.0\n433\t    biavr_verify_rate: 0.68\n434\t    random_p50_verify_rate: 0.5\n435\t    confidence_verify_rate: 0.55\n436\t    biavr_cost_reduction: 0.28\n437\t  result_rationale: Median 档下各 baseline 表现：(1) No-verify 比 always-on 低 9pp（verification\n438\t    有 value 但不 dramatic），(2) Random-p50 在 50% verify rate 下只丢 5pp（说明 selective 的 marginal\n439\t    value 有限——random 就能保留大部分 benefit），(3) Confidence threshold 与 random 接近（model confidence\n440\t    不是 good proxy for informativeness at 30% success level）。B-IAVR 优于 random 和 confidence\n441\t    但优势小（1-2pp at matched cost），因为 action-change signal 本身 noisy。Pareto frontier analysis\n442\t    中 B-IAVR 不 clearly dominate——接近 random baseline 的 performance。这削弱了 Claim 3 的独立贡献。\n443\t  tables:\n444\t  - title: Full comparison on held-out val set\n445\t    columns:\n446\t    - method\n447\t    - success\n448\t    - verify_rate\n449\t    - rel_cost\n450\t    - success/cost\n451\t    rows:\n452\t    - - always-on\n453\t      - 31%\n454\t      - 100%\n455\t      - '1.00'\n456\t      - '0.31'\n457\t    - - B-IAVR\n458\t      - 27%\n459\t      - 68%\n460\t      - '0.72'\n461\t      - '0.375'\n462\t    - - random-p=0.5\n463\t      - 26%\n464\t      - 50%\n465\t      - '0.55'\n466\t      - '0.473'\n467\t    - - confidence-thresh\n468\t      - 25%\n469\t      - 55%\n470\t      - '0.60'\n471\t      - '0.417'\n472\t    - - no-verify\n473\t      - 22%\n474\t      - 0%\n475\t      - '0.45'\n476\t      - '0.489'\n477\t  figures_description:\n478\t  - 'Figure: Pareto plot (x=cost, y=success). B-IAVR slightly above random/confidence\n479\t    curve but not dramatically. Always-on is upper-right anchor.'\n480\t  analysis: B-IAVR 在 absolute Pareto efficiency 上优于 baselines 但 margin 小。Random baseline\n481\t    意外 competitive，说明 'when to verify' 的 learned signal 价值有限 at this performance level。Paper\n482\t    需要 downplay Claim 3 到 'preliminary evidence that learned selective policy outperforms\n483\t    naive baselines' level。可能需要 Plan B（更强 base agent）才能让 selective verification story\n484\t    有说服力。\n485\t- name: No-verify ablation\n486\t  plan_id: plan_009\n487\t  description: Episode-level GRPO without self-verification, lower bound\n488\t  expected_results:\n489\t    success_rate: 0.22\n490\t    action_is_valid: 0.58\n491\t    vs_always_on_delta: -9\n492\t    avg_episode_length: 18\n493\t  result_rationale: No-verify 比 always-on 低 9pp（median 档 expectation）。Verification\n494\t    的主要价值在于 error recovery——检测并修正 invalid/ineffective actions。在 30% success 的 agent\n495\t    中，roughly 1/3 的 success 来自 verification-triggered correction（30% × 0.3 ≈ 9pp contribution）。但\n496\t    delta 只有 9pp 而非更大，因为：(1) 72% verification 是 confirmatory（不改变行为），(2) 部分 action\n497\t    change 是 noise 而非 correction，(3) 一些任务不需要 verification 就能完成（simple pick tasks）。这验证了\n498\t    verification 有 value 但也说明 always-on 的 inefficiency（72% 浪费）。\n499\t  tables: []\n500\t  figures_description: []\n501\t  analysis: 9pp delta 证明 verification 有 non-trivial value，支撑了 selective verification\n502\t    的 motivation。但 delta 不够大（<10pp），使 cost-saving story 的 potential 有限——即使完美 selective，最多能恢复\n503\t    9pp 中的大部分。\n504\t- name: Entropy-controlled action-change analysis\n505\t  plan_id: plan_010\n506\t  description: Partial correlation of action-change with success after controlling\n507\t    for policy entropy\n508\t  expected_results:\n509\t    raw_correlation: 0.15\n510\t    partial_correlation_entropy_controlled: 0.11\n511\t    p_value: 0.038\n512\t    high_entropy_stratum_correlation: 0.08\n513\t    low_entropy_stratum_correlation: 0.14\n514\t    medium_entropy_stratum_correlation: 0.12\n515\t  result_rationale: Median 档定义 action-change partial correlation 0.10-0.20，取 0.11\n516\t    after controlling entropy。Raw correlation 从 0.15 降到 0.11（entropy 解释了部分 variance，说明\n517\t    high-entropy states 确实倾向于产生 action change 而非 informed correction）。P-value 0.038\n518\t    刚过 significance threshold 但不 compelling（reviewer 可能要求 Bonferroni correction 后不再\n519\t    significant）。Low-entropy stratum correlation 更高（0.14）说明在 confident states 中 action\n520\t    change 更可能是 informative signal，而 high-entropy 中更可能是 noise。这是 partial defense 但不是\n521\t    strong evidence。\n522\t  tables:\n523\t  - title: Stratified correlation analysis\n524\t    columns:\n525\t    - entropy_stratum\n526\t    - n\n527\t    - action_change_rate\n528\t    - correlation\n529\t    - p_value\n530\t    rows:\n531\t    - - low (<0.1)\n532\t      - '180'\n533\t      - 18%\n534\t      - '0.14'\n535\t      - '0.06'\n536\t    - - medium (0.1-0.3)\n537\t      - '250'\n538\t      - 28%\n539\t      - '0.12'\n540\t      - '0.05'\n541\t    - - high (>0.3)\n542\t      - '120'\n543\t      - 42%\n544\t      - '0.08'\n545\t      - '0.38'\n546\t  figures_description:\n547\t  - 'Figure: Three scatter plots (one per entropy stratum) showing action-change vs\n548\t    episode success. Regression lines with CI bands.'\n549\t  analysis: 'Signal exists but is weak and barely significant. Defense against ''action\n550\t    change = noise'' is partial: can say ''signal persists after entropy control''\n551\t    but effect size is small. Honest paper would acknowledge this as limitation and\n552\t    position action-change as ''best available proxy'' rather than ''validated signal''.'\n553\t- name: 'Causal intervention: random vs verification-triggered changes'\n554\t  plan_id: plan_011\n555\t  description: Inject random action changes vs verification-triggered, compare success\n556\t  expected_results:\n557\t    verification_triggered_success: 0.32\n558\t    random_triggered_success: 0.24\n559\t    no_change_baseline_success: 0.28\n560\t    delta_triggered_vs_random: 8\n561\t    delta_triggered_vs_nochange: 4\n562\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档下 verification-triggered changes 比 random changes 好 8pp。原因：verification\n563\t    过程给 model 额外 context（重新审视 state），使得 change 更 informed。但 delta 只有 8pp 而非 15+pp（strong\n564\t    档），因为：(1) 30% success agent 的 verification quality 中等（不是所有 verification-triggered\n565\t    change 都是 correct），(2) random change 有时碰巧也有用（ALFWorld action space 有限，random valid\n566\t    action 有 non-trivial hit rate），(3) ''no change baseline'' 成功率 28% 意味着很多 episodes\n567\t    不需要 correction 就能 succeed/fail。Interesting finding: triggered > no-change > random?\n568\t    No — triggered > no-change, random < no-change. Random changes 实际上 hurt（从 28%\n569\t    → 24%），verification-triggered 才是 helpful。'\n570\t  tables:\n571\t  - title: Causal intervention results\n572\t    columns:\n573\t    - condition\n574\t    - success_rate\n575\t    - n_episodes\n576\t    - vs_baseline\n577\t    rows:\n578\t    - - verification-triggered change\n579\t      - 32%\n580\t      - '200'\n581\t      - +4pp\n582\t    - - no change (baseline)\n583\t      - 28%\n584\t      - '200'\n585\t      - —\n586\t    - - random change (same rate)\n587\t      - 24%\n588\t      - '200'\n589\t      - -4pp\n590\t  figures_description:\n591\t  - 'Figure: Bar chart with confidence intervals. Verification-triggered > baseline\n592\t    > random. Stars for significance.'\n593\t  analysis: Provides causal evidence that verification adds value (not just noise).\n594\t    But effect size moderate (+4pp vs baseline, +8pp vs random). Combined with entropy\n595\t    analysis, forms a 'converging evidence' argument for action-change being a real\n596\t    signal, even if weak individually.\n597\t- name: Reward signal ablation\n598\t  plan_id: plan_012\n599\t  description: B-IAVR with action-change vs random-trigger vs confidence-based reward\n600\t  expected_results:\n601\t    action_change_success: 0.27\n602\t    action_change_verify_rate: 0.68\n603\t    random_trigger_success: 0.25\n604\t    random_trigger_verify_rate: 0.62\n605\t    confidence_reward_success: 0.24\n606\t    confidence_verify_rate: 0.7\n607\t  result_rationale: Median 档下 action-change reward 优于 alternatives 但 margin 小。Action-change\n608\t    (27%, verify 68%) vs random-trigger (25%, verify 62%) delta = 2pp success, +6pp\n609\t    verify rate。原因：(1) random trigger reward 无 informative signal，模型学到的 verify 策略接近\n610\t    uniform random，(2) confidence-based reward 在 1.7B model 上不好估计（model 的 logit calibration\n611\t    差，confidence 不 correlate well with actual uncertainty），(3) action-change 虽然 noisy\n612\t    但至少有 partial signal（r=0.11）。Margin 小因为 base signal 本身弱——在 strong 档下差异会更明显。\n613\t  tables:\n614\t  - title: Reward signal comparison\n615\t    columns:\n616\t    - reward_type\n617\t    - success\n618\t    - verify_rate\n619\t    - cost_reduction\n620\t    - training_stability\n621\t    rows:\n622\t    - - action-change (ours)\n623\t      - 27%\n624\t      - 68%\n625\t      - 28%\n626\t      - moderate (converges step 40)\n627\t    - - random trigger\n628\t      - 25%\n629\t      - 62%\n630\t      - 35%\n631\t      - unstable (high variance)\n632\t    - - confidence-based\n633\t      - 24%\n634\t      - 70%\n635\t      - 26%\n636\t      - slow convergence\n637\t  figures_description: []\n638\t  analysis: Action-change is best but advantage is modest (2-3pp). Paper can claim\n639\t    'action-change outperforms baselines' but the weak margin means a reviewer could\n640\t    argue the differences are within noise. Need to frame carefully with error bars\n641\t    and multiple seeds.\n642\t- name: ARES reproduction + comparison\n643\t  plan_id: plan_013\n644\t  description: Reproduce ARES SFT router on ALFWorld, head-to-head with B-IAVR\n645\t  expected_results:\n646\t    ares_success: 0.26\n647\t    ares_verify_rate: 0.58\n648\t    ares_cost_reduction: 0.38\n649\t    biavr_success: 0.27\n650\t    biavr_verify_rate: 0.68\n651\t    biavr_cost_reduction: 0.28\n652\t    delta_success: 1\n653\t    delta_cost: -10\n654\t  result_rationale: ARES 使用 SFT router（从 oracle labels 学 when to verify），在 cost reduction\n655\t    上优于 B-IAVR（38% vs 28%）但 success 相近（26% vs 27%）。原因：(1) SFT 有 direct supervision\n656\t    signal（teacher-labeled 'should verify here'），训练更 clean，(2) 但 SFT labels 是 frozen（从一个\n657\t    checkpoint 生成），不 adapt to policy improvement，所以 success 不如 RL-trained 的 B-IAVR，(3)\n658\t    ARES 的 continuous effort allocation 在 ALFWorld binary 场景中退化为 threshold，效果有限。Head-to-head\n659\t    中 B-IAVR 不 clearly dominate ARES — 不同 trade-off point。这削弱了 'B-IAVR dominates'\n660\t    的 claim。\n661\t  tables:\n662\t  - title: ARES vs B-IAVR head-to-head\n663\t    columns:\n664\t    - method\n665\t    - success\n666\t    - verify_rate\n667\t    - cost_reduction\n668\t    - training_data_needed\n669\t    rows:\n670\t    - - ARES (SFT router)\n671\t      - 26%\n672\t      - 58%\n673\t      - 38%\n674\t      - oracle labels required\n675\t    - - B-IAVR (RL)\n676\t      - 27%\n677\t      - 68%\n678\t      - 28%\n679\t      - no labels (self-supervised)\n680\t    - - always-on\n681\t      - 31%\n682\t      - 100%\n683\t      - 0%\n684\t      - —\n685\t  figures_description:\n686\t  - 'Figure: Pareto plot with ARES and B-IAVR as labeled points. Neither dominates\n687\t    the other — ARES better on cost, B-IAVR better on success.'\n688\t  analysis: ARES comparison doesn't favor our method on cost reduction. Differentiation\n689\t    must come from methodology (no oracle labels needed, RL-based adaptation) rather\n690\t    than performance numbers. Paper should frame as 'comparable performance without\n691\t    supervision' rather than 'superior performance'.\n692\t- name: ScienceWorld transfer\n693\t  plan_id: plan_014\n694\t  description: Episode-level vs step-independent on ScienceWorld environment\n695\t  expected_results:\n696\t    episode_level_success: 0.18\n697\t    step_independent_success: 0.04\n698\t    improvement_ratio: 4.5\n699\t    episode_level_std: 0.05\n700\t    convergence_slower: true\n701\t    steps_to_plateau: 25\n702\t  result_rationale: Median 档下 transfer 到 ScienceWorld 仍显示 episode-level 优势（4.5x）但\n703\t    absolute performance 较低（18% vs ALFWorld 的 30%）。原因：(1) ScienceWorld 比 ALFWorld\n704\t    更复杂（更长 episode、更大 action space、partial observability），(2) 1.7B 模型在 science reasoning\n705\t    上能力有限，(3) step-independent 在更长 horizon（ScienceWorld 40-50 步）下崩溃更严重（4% vs ALFWorld\n706\t    的 3%），(4) 收敛更慢因为 reward 更 sparse。Results 支持 generalization claim 但 18% absolute\n707\t    performance 不算 impressive。\n708\t  tables:\n709\t  - title: ScienceWorld transfer results\n710\t    columns:\n711\t    - method\n712\t    - success_rate\n713\t    - improvement_vs_step_ind\n714\t    rows:\n715\t    - - step-independent (h=2)\n716\t      - 4%\n717\t      - baseline\n718\t    - - step-independent (h=10)\n719\t      - 9%\n720\t      - 2.3x\n721\t    - - episode-level GRPO\n722\t      - 18%\n723\t      - 4.5x\n724\t  figures_description:\n725\t  - 'Figure: Learning curves for episode-level vs step-independent on ScienceWorld.\n726\t    Slower convergence but same qualitative pattern as ALFWorld.'\n727\t  analysis: 'Supports generalization: dual mechanism failure is not ALFWorld-specific.\n728\t    But low absolute numbers (18%) limit the impact claim. Paper can use this as ''consistent\n729\t    across environments'' evidence for Claim 1 diagnostic.'\n730\t- name: 7B model scaling verification\n731\t  plan_id: plan_015\n732\t  description: Episode-level vs step-independent on Qwen3-7B\n733\t  expected_results:\n734\t    episode_7b_success: 0.42\n735\t    step_ind_7b_success: 0.08\n736\t    improvement_ratio: 5.25\n737\t    episode_7b_vs_1.7b_delta: 10\n738\t    step_ind_7b_vs_1.7b_delta: 5\n739\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档下 7B 模型 episode-level 达到 42%（vs 1.7B 的 32%），step-independent\n740\t    仍 collapse 到 8%（vs 1.7B 的 3%，7B 有更好 base capabilities 所以 collapse 后仍保留一些）。Episode-level\n741\t    的 10pp 提升来自 larger model 的 better base reasoning/planning。Step-independent 的 slight\n742\t    improvement（8% vs 3%）因为 7B 在短 window 内也能做更好的 local decisions，但 sign misattribution\n743\t    仍然阻止真正的 improvement。Key finding: scaling 不能 fix step-independent 的 structural\n744\t    problem（8% 仍远低于 episode-level 的 42%）。'\n745\t  tables:\n746\t  - title: Model size scaling\n747\t    columns:\n748\t    - model\n749\t    - episode-level\n750\t    - step-ind (h=2)\n751\t    - ratio\n752\t    rows:\n753\t    - - Qwen3-1.7B\n754\t      - 32%\n755\t      - 3%\n756\t      - 10.7x\n757\t    - - Qwen3-7B\n758\t      - 42%\n759\t      - 8%\n760\t      - 5.3x\n761\t  figures_description:\n762\t  - 'Figure: 2x2 comparison (model size × training method). Episode-level scales well;\n763\t    step-independent remains broken regardless of size.'\n764\t  analysis: 'Supports Claim 1: step-independent failure is structural, not a model\n765\t    capacity issue. 7B cannot compensate for broken credit assignment. Episode-level\n766\t    benefits from scale as expected. Ratio decreases (10.7x→5.3x) but absolute gap\n767\t    increases (29pp→34pp).'\n768\t- name: Per-task-type breakdown\n769\t  plan_id: plan_016\n770\t  description: ALFWorld success breakdown by task type for episode-level\n771\t  expected_results:\n772\t    put_success: 0.4\n773\t    clean_success: 0.32\n774\t    heat_success: 0.28\n775\t    cool_success: 0.3\n776\t    examine_success: 0.18\n777\t    pick_two_success: 0.15\n778\t    correlation_with_length: -0.72\n779\t    short_task_advantage: 12\n780\t  result_rationale: 'Median 档下 per-task 差异明显：simple tasks（put: 40%）远好于 complex tasks（examine:\n781\t    18%, pick_two: 15%）。原因：(1) 短 episode tasks（put 通常 10-15 步）在 episode-level 下 credit\n782\t    assignment 更 focused（fewer actions dilute the signal），(2) Complex tasks 需要 multi-step\n783\t    planning（先找 object、再找 tool、再执行），30% overall success 的 agent 在需要 3+ correct decisions\n784\t    的 task 上 success 急剧下降，(3) pick_two 需要 remember 两个 target objects——working memory\n785\t    challenge for 1.7B。Length-success correlation -0.72 confirms episode complexity\n786\t    is key difficulty factor。'\n787\t  tables:\n788\t  - title: Per-task breakdown (episode-level, step 15)\n789\t    columns:\n790\t    - task_type\n791\t    - success\n792\t    - avg_steps\n793\t    - action_is_valid\n794\t    - n_val\n795\t    rows:\n796\t    - - put\n797\t      - 40%\n798\t      - '12.3'\n799\t      - 62%\n800\t      - '10'\n801\t    - - clean\n802\t      - 32%\n803\t      - '18.7'\n804\t      - 55%\n805\t      - '6'\n806\t    - - cool\n807\t      - 30%\n808\t      - '16.2'\n809\t      - 58%\n810\t      - '4'\n811\t    - - heat\n812\t      - 28%\n813\t      - '17.8'\n814\t      - 53%\n815\t      - '4'\n816\t    - - examine\n817\t      - 18%\n818\t      - '24.5'\n819\t      - 48%\n820\t      - '3'\n821\t    - - pick_two\n822\t      - 15%\n823\t      - '28.1'\n824\t      - 45%\n825\t      - '5'\n826\t  figures_description:\n827\t  - 'Figure: Scatter plot of task avg_steps vs success_rate with fitted regression\n828\t    line. Clear negative correlation (-0.72).'\n829\t  analysis: 'Confirms intuition: episode-level advantage is largest for simpler tasks\n830\t    where credit can be assigned more cleanly. Complex tasks remain challenging even\n831\t    with episode-level training — potential direction for future work (hierarchical\n832\t    RL or subgoal decomposition). Useful for paper''s ''limitation'' section.'\n833\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"03539836-91ef-4e0c-a664-f46ce3e7053e","uuid":"1044ba3c-25ec-4438-8de9-9ec136230432","timestamp":"2026-05-17T12:46:45.580Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_1/projects/cost-verify-agent-rl/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260517T121256/median/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: 重心从 'dual contribution' 转向 'diagnostic contribution + preliminary\n  application'。核心贡献是双机制诊断的系统分析（sign misattribution + information loss），episode-level\n  GRPO 定位为 minimum viable fix 而非 optimal solution（GAE 可能更优 5-15pp），selective verification\n  作为 preliminary downstream application 呈现（claim 降为 moderate-to-weak）。需要补充 mechanistic\n  analysis 深度和 community practice survey 来弥补 application 侧的弱势。\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: Context window h-sweep ablation\n  plan_id: plan_002\n  description: h={2, 5, 10, 20, full} × 3 seeds each, 15 steps per run\n  expected_results:\n    h2_mean_success: 0.02\n    h2_std: 0.02\n    h5_mean_success: 0.08\n    h5_std: 0.04\n    h10_mean_success: 0.18\n    h10_std: 0.06\n    h20_mean_success: 0.28\n    h20_std: 0.05\n    full_mean_success: 0.34\n    full_std: 0.05\n    cliff_location: h=5→h=2 (sharp), h=10→h=5 (moderate)\n    h2_collapse_rate: 0.67\n    h5_collapse_rate: 0.33\n    h10_collapse_rate: 0.0\n  result_rationale: Median 档下 cliff 边界模糊：h=10 有时 collapse 有时不（0/3 seeds collapse 但方差大），h=5\n    是 unstable zone（1/3 collapse），h=2 几乎确定 collapse（2/3 seeds）。与 strong 档的 clean cliff（h=5\n    以下全崩）不同，这里存在 seed-dependent 的边界效应。原因：sign misattribution 的影响程度取决于 episode 长度分布——短\n    episode（如 pick 任务 10 步内完成）在 h=10 下 window 数少，misattribution 较轻；长 episode（examine\n    30+ 步）在 h=10 下仍有显著 misattribution。Seed 间的差异来自 initial rollout 的任务分布随机性。full 模式收敛到\n    34% 而非更高（median 档上限 44%），因为 1.7B 模型 capacity 和 ALFWorld 的 exploration 难度形成了 soft\n    ceiling。\n  tables:\n  - title: H-sweep results (15 steps, 3 seeds)\n    columns:\n    - h\n    - seed1\n    - seed2\n    - seed3\n    - mean±std\n    - collapse?\n    rows:\n    - - '2'\n      - 0%\n      - 4%\n      - 3%\n      - 2.3±2.1\n      - 2/3 collapse by step 5\n    - - '5'\n      - 12%\n      - 6%\n      - 5%\n      - 7.7±3.8\n      - 1/3 partial collapse\n    - - '10'\n      - 22%\n      - 14%\n      - 19%\n      - 18.3±4.0\n      - 0/3 collapse\n    - - '20'\n      - 32%\n      - 24%\n      - 28%\n      - 28.0±4.0\n      - 0/3\n    - - full\n      - 38%\n      - 30%\n      - 34%\n      - 34.0±4.0\n      - 0/3\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure: Line plot with error bars, x=h (log scale), y=val_success_rate. Shows\n    monotonic improvement but cliff is gradual (h=2→5) rather than sharp step function.\n    Shaded region = seed std. Annotation: ''cliff zone h∈[2,5]'' with dashed boundary.'\n  analysis: Cliff 存在但不如预期 clean。Reviewer 可能质疑 'catastrophic' 一词——h=5 仍有 8% 而非 0%。需要调整叙述为\n    'severe degradation zone' 而非 'binary cliff'。个别 seed 在 h=10 表现不稳定（14% vs 22%）增加了\n    std，但趋势方向一致。这支持 Claim 1 但需要降低 language 的绝对性。\n- name: Multi-seed replication (5 seeds)\n  plan_id: plan_003\n  description: 4 additional seeds for episode-level config, report mean±std at step\n    15\n  expected_results:\n    seed1_success: 0.28\n    seed2_success: 0.34\n    seed3_success: 0.38\n    seed4_success: 0.31\n    seed5_success: 0.22\n    mean_success: 0.306\n    std_success: 0.059\n    min_success: 0.22\n    max_success: 0.38\n    convergence_step_range: 10-15\n  result_rationale: Median 档定义 std 4-7pp，这里取 5.9pp。5 seeds 中有一个 outlier（seed5=22%）拉低均值并增大方差。原因：episode-level\n    GRPO 对 initial rollout quality 敏感——如果前几步 rollout 恰好采样到较难的任务子集（如 examine_in_light），early\n    gradient 信号弱，后续收敛慢。大部分 seed 在 28-38% 范围内（趋势一致），但 seed5 的偏离使 CI 较宽。这足以支持 'episode-level\n    works' 的 claim，但 reviewer 会注意到 22% outlier 并要求解释。\n  tables:\n  - title: Multi-seed episode-level results at step 15\n    columns:\n    - seed\n    - val_success\n    - train_success\n    - action_is_valid\n    - pass_at_8\n    rows:\n    - - 1 (original)\n      - 28.1%\n      - 43.8%\n      - 54.5%\n      - 92.9%\n    - - '2'\n      - 34.4%\n      - 50.0%\n      - 61.2%\n      - 95.3%\n    - - '3'\n      - 37.5%\n      - 53.1%\n      - 63.8%\n      - 96.1%\n    - - '4'\n      - 31.3%\n      - 46.9%\n      - 58.7%\n      - 93.8%\n    - - '5'\n      - 21.9%\n      - 34.4%\n      - 48.2%\n      - 87.5%\n    - - mean±std\n      - 30.6±5.9%\n      - 45.6±7.1%\n      - 57.3±6.1%\n      - 93.1±3.4%\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure: Box plot of 5 seeds with individual points overlaid. Median line at 31.3%,\n    box spans 28.1-34.4% (IQR), whiskers to 22-38%. Annotate seed 5 as potential outlier.'\n  analysis: Std=5.9pp 处于 median 档范围（4-7pp）。趋势一致（所有 seed > step-independent baseline\n    的 0-6%），但绝对方差偏大，使 95% CI 为 [30.6±5.3pp] = [25.3, 35.9]。不能 claim '≥40% success'\n    — mean 只有 30.6%。Paper 需要 acknowledge variance 并定位 episode-level 为 'consistent\n    improvement over step-independent' 而非 'strong agent'。\n- name: GAE baseline comparison\n  plan_id: plan_003b\n  description: GAE(λ=0.95,γ=1.0) 和 GAE(λ=1.0,γ=1.0) vs episode-level GRPO, 15 steps\n    × 3 seeds\n  expected_results:\n    gae_095_mean_success: 0.4\n    gae_095_std: 0.05\n    gae_100_mean_success: 0.37\n    gae_100_std: 0.04\n    episode_grpo_mean_success: 0.32\n    episode_grpo_std: 0.05\n    gae_095_vs_episode_delta: 8\n    gae_100_vs_episode_delta: 5\n    step_independent_mean_success: 0.03\n  result_rationale: Median 档定义 GAE vs episode-level delta 为 5-15pp，这里 GAE(0.95) 领先\n    8pp。GAE 能做 per-token credit assignment（通过 critic），而 episode-level GRPO 给所有 token\n    同一 advantage。在 30-step episode 中，GAE 能区分 'step 5 的 go to drawer 是好的' vs 'step\n    20 的 random action 是差的'，而 GRPO 无法区分。但 GAE 优势有限（非 dramatic）因为：(1) critic 在 1.7B\n    模型上估计 V(s) 噪声大（multi-turn text state 难以准确估值），(2) ALFWorld 的 reward 仍是 binary sparse，critic\n    bootstrapping 在 sparse reward 下不稳定。GAE(λ=1.0) 接近 Monte Carlo（与 GRPO episode-level\n    语义相近但有 critic variance reduction），所以 delta 较小（5pp）。这个结果对 paper 是 double-edged：证明\n    per-token credit 有价值（GAE > GRPO），但也说明 episode-level GRPO 不是最优解。需要定位为 'minimum\n    viable fix, not optimal'。\n  tables:\n  - title: Training method comparison at step 15 (3 seeds)\n    columns:\n    - method\n    - val_success\n    - std\n    - vs step-ind delta\n    rows:\n    - - Step-independent (h=2)\n      - 3±2%\n      - 2pp\n      - baseline\n    - - Step-independent (h=10)\n      - 18±4%\n      - 4pp\n      - +15pp\n    - - Episode-level GRPO\n      - 32±5%\n      - 5pp\n      - +29pp\n    - - GAE(λ=1.0, γ=1.0)\n      - 37±4%\n      - 4pp\n      - +34pp\n    - - GAE(λ=0.95, γ=1.0)\n      - 40±5%\n      - 5pp\n      - +37pp\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure: Bar chart with error bars. Clear ordering: step-ind << episode-GRPO <\n    GAE. Annotation: ''per-token credit provides additional 5-8pp over episode-level''.'\n  analysis: GAE 优势证实 per-token credit assignment 有额外价值，这削弱了 'episode-level 就够了' 的\n    strong claim。Paper 需要 reframe：episode-level 是 zero-cost fix（无需 critic 实现），GAE\n    是 upper bound 但需要额外 engineering（critic head + training stability）。Diagnostic 贡献不受影响——两者都远超\n    step-independent，证明 dual mechanism 是真正的 failure mode。\n- name: Episode-level + valid_action_bonus plateau-breaker\n  plan_id: plan_003c\n  description: Episode-level + valid_action_bonus=0.05, 15 steps\n  expected_results:\n    success_rate_step15: 0.34\n    action_is_valid_step15: 0.72\n    valid_bonus_reward_ratio: 0.15\n    no_gaming_detected: true\n    vs_vanilla_episode_delta: 4\n  result_rationale: Median 档下 episode-level 本身 plateau 在 30-34%。加 valid_action_bonus\n    后：(1) 不发生 gaming（exp013f 的 gaming 是 step-independent-specific，因为 per-window 优化可以独立\n    maximize bonus 而忽略 task reward；episode-level 下 bonus 只是 total trajectory reward\n    的一小部分），(2) action_is_valid 从 55% 提升到 72%（学会更好的 format 但未达 80% target），(3) success\n    从 30% 提升到 34%（小幅改善，breaking plateau 效果有限）。原因：valid action 是 necessary but not\n    sufficient for success——模型已经学到了大部分 valid action pattern，剩余的 failure 来自 exploration\n    strategy 而非 format 错误。Bonus 帮助但不足以突破根本性的 exploration bottleneck。\n  tables:\n  - title: Valid action bonus effect (episode-level)\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - vanilla\n    - +bonus\n    - delta\n    rows:\n    - - val_success\n      - 30.6%\n      - 34.4%\n      - +3.8pp\n    - - action_is_valid\n      - 57.3%\n      - 72.1%\n      - +14.8pp\n    - - reward_mean\n      - '3.06'\n      - '4.12'\n      - '+1.06'\n    - - gaming_detected\n      - 'no'\n      - 'no'\n      - '-'\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 'Confirms D056 insight: dense reward gaming 是 step-independent-specific。但\n    success 提升有限（+4pp），不足以单独作为 plateau-breaker。可能需要组合其他方法（如 curriculum 或 Self-Guide\n    reward）来突破 40%。作为 ablation 有价值但非 main story。'\n- name: Credit assignment mechanism empirical verification\n  plan_id: plan_004\n  description: Per-window advantage logging from h=2 runs, sign/magnitude analysis\n  expected_results:\n    sign_vs_outcome_correlation: 0.87\n    sign_vs_local_quality_correlation: 0.12\n    magnitude_position_decay_r2: 0.75\n    episode_level_sign_variance: 0.0\n    episode_level_magnitude_variance: 0.02\n    success_episodes_all_positive_pct: 0.92\n    failure_episodes_all_negative_pct: 0.89\n    gamma_k_fit_coefficient: 0.93\n  result_rationale: Median 档定义 sign-outcome correlation 0.80-0.95，取 0.87。不完美（非 1.0）的原因：(1)\n    GRPO 的 group normalization 引入噪声——同一 group 内如果有多个 success episodes，normalization\n    后部分 success episode 的 advantage 可能为负（因为相对排名），(2) 极短 episode（2-3 步就成功/失败）中 window\n    数太少，统计不稳定。Sign vs local quality correlation = 0.12（非零但弱），因为存在 confound：好的 local\n    actions 确实倾向于出现在成功 episode 中（相关但非因果），但这种 correlation 远弱于 sign-outcome correlation（0.87\n    vs 0.12）。Magnitude decay R²=0.75 而非更高，因为 reward normalization 和 group composition\n    增加了 position-magnitude 关系的噪声。Episode-level 下 variance 为 0（by design，所有 token 同一\n    advantage）。\n  tables:\n  - title: Mechanism verification results\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - observed\n    - theory predicts\n    - interpretation\n    rows:\n    - - sign↔outcome r\n      - '0.87'\n      - ~1.0\n      - Direction mostly correct, noise from GRPO normalization\n    - - sign↔local_quality r\n      - '0.12'\n      - ~0.0\n      - Weak confound exists but not causal\n    - - γ^k decay R²\n      - '0.75'\n      - high\n      - Magnitude decays with position, moderate fit\n    - - episode-level sign var\n      - '0.0'\n      - '0.0'\n      - No position-dependent sign (by design)\n    - - success→all positive\n      - 92%\n      - 100%\n      - GRPO group norm creates exceptions\n    - - failure→all negative\n      - 89%\n      - 100%\n      - Same GRPO norm effect\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure 2a: Scatter plot of (episode_outcome, advantage_sign) for 500 windows\n    from h=2 runs. Clear clustering but ~10% of points in ''wrong'' quadrant. Color\n    by position.'\n  - 'Figure 2b: Advantage magnitude vs window position (normalized). Fitted γ^k curve\n    overlaid. R²=0.75 annotated.'\n  - 'Figure 2c: Episode-level control — flat line (all tokens same advantage), demonstrating\n    absence of sign/magnitude variation.'\n  analysis: 'Core mechanism confirmed but with noise: sign misattribution 方向正确（r=0.87）但非\n    deterministic。Paper 需要用 ''predominantly determined by'' 而非 ''entirely determined\n    by''。Partial correlation with local quality (0.12) means a reviewer could argue\n    ''some useful signal gets through'' — defense: 0.12 vs 0.87 shows signal is overwhelmed\n    by outcome-driven noise，且 gradient direction (reinforce/suppress) 仍主要由 outcome\n    决定。这对 diagnostic contribution 足够，但需要 careful language。'\n- name: Action-change statistics from always-on runs\n  plan_id: plan_005\n  description: Collect action-change rates from exp029 checkpoints\n  expected_results:\n    overall_action_change_rate: 0.28\n    confirmatory_rate: 0.72\n    action_change_success_correlation: 0.15\n    per_task_put_change_rate: 0.22\n    per_task_clean_change_rate: 0.31\n    per_task_heat_change_rate: 0.35\n    per_task_examine_change_rate: 0.38\n    early_step_change_rate: 0.35\n    late_step_change_rate: 0.2\n  result_rationale: Median 档下 episode-level 训练到 30% success，模型的 verification 质量中等。Action-change\n    rate 28%（72% confirmatory）因为：(1) 模型 confidence 中等——不像 untrained 模型那样 always change，也不像\n    strong model 那样 rarely change，(2) 30% success 意味着大部分 trajectory 仍在失败，verification\n    后模型倾向于保持原有 plan（因为没学到更好的替代）。Correlation 0.15（低于 strong 档的 0.3+）因为 action change\n    有时是 noise（模型 uncertain 时随机切换）而非 informed correction。Per-task 差异：complex tasks（examine,\n    heat）change 率高因为 action space 更大、uncertainty 更高。\n  tables:\n  - title: Action-change statistics by task type\n    columns:\n    - task_type\n    - change_rate\n    - change→success_rate\n    - no_change→success_rate\n    rows:\n    - - put\n      - 22%\n      - 35%\n      - 28%\n    - - clean\n      - 31%\n      - 30%\n      - 25%\n    - - heat\n      - 35%\n      - 33%\n      - 22%\n    - - cool\n      - 30%\n      - 32%\n      - 24%\n    - - examine\n      - 38%\n      - 28%\n      - 18%\n    - - overall\n      - 28%\n      - 32%\n      - 25%\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure: Stacked bar showing confirmatory vs corrective verification per task\n    type. Annotation: 72% of verifications do not change behavior.'\n  analysis: Confirms hypothesis that most verification is confirmatory. Correlation\n    with success (0.15) is positive but weak — this is the foundation for action-change\n    reward but the weak signal means selective verification training will be noisy.\n    Need to acknowledge this limitation upfront.\n- name: B-IAVR selective verification training\n  plan_id: plan_007\n  description: Episode-level GRPO with verify/skip decision, action-change reward\n  expected_results:\n    final_success_rate: 0.27\n    verification_rate: 0.68\n    verification_rate_reduction: 0.32\n    success_delta_vs_always_on: -5\n    training_steps_to_converge: 40\n    reward_convergence: noisy plateau after step 25\n    action_is_valid: 0.65\n  result_rationale: Median 档定义 selective verification rate ↓20-40%，取 32%。Success delta\n    为 -5pp（3-8pp 范围内）。原因：(1) action-change reward signal 本身较弱（correlation 0.15），训练\n    selective policy 的信号不 clean，(2) 模型在 'should I verify?' 决策上学到了粗糙的 heuristic（如 'verify\n    after go to X'）但没学到精细的 uncertainty estimation，(3) 减少 32% verification 意味着在一些 informative\n    verification 场景也错误跳过了，导致 5pp success drop。训练过程 noisy（action-change reward 的方差大），convergence\n    慢。这是 'preliminary evidence' 而非 'strong demonstration' — 够写一段 results 但不够支撑 strong\n    claim。\n  tables:\n  - title: B-IAVR training trajectory\n    columns:\n    - step\n    - success\n    - verify_rate\n    - cost_tokens\n    rows:\n    - - '0'\n      - 30%\n      - 100%\n      - 1.0x\n    - - '10'\n      - 28%\n      - 85%\n      - 0.88x\n    - - '20'\n      - 26%\n      - 74%\n      - 0.78x\n    - - '30'\n      - 27%\n      - 70%\n      - 0.74x\n    - - '40'\n      - 27%\n      - 68%\n      - 0.72x\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure: Dual-axis plot showing success rate (left, relatively flat ~27%) and\n    verification rate (right, declining from 100% to 68%). Trade-off visible.'\n  analysis: Verification rate 下降 32% 但 success 也下降 5pp。这不是 'free lunch' — 是 explicit\n    trade-off。Claim 3 需要大幅降级：从 'matches always-on at reduced cost' 变为 'achieves moderate\n    cost reduction with modest performance sacrifice'。作为 preliminary application 可接受但不是\n    paper 的 selling point。\n- name: Selective verification full comparison\n  plan_id: plan_008\n  description: Always-on / B-IAVR / no-verify / random-p / confidence baseline comparison\n  expected_results:\n    always_on_success: 0.31\n    biavr_success: 0.27\n    no_verify_success: 0.22\n    random_p50_success: 0.26\n    confidence_threshold_success: 0.25\n    always_on_verify_rate: 1.0\n    biavr_verify_rate: 0.68\n    random_p50_verify_rate: 0.5\n    confidence_verify_rate: 0.55\n    biavr_cost_reduction: 0.28\n  result_rationale: Median 档下各 baseline 表现：(1) No-verify 比 always-on 低 9pp（verification\n    有 value 但不 dramatic），(2) Random-p50 在 50% verify rate 下只丢 5pp（说明 selective 的 marginal\n    value 有限——random 就能保留大部分 benefit），(3) Confidence threshold 与 random 接近（model confidence\n    不是 good proxy for informativeness at 30% success level）。B-IAVR 优于 random 和 confidence\n    但优势小（1-2pp at matched cost），因为 action-change signal 本身 noisy。Pareto frontier analysis\n    中 B-IAVR 不 clearly dominate——接近 random baseline 的 performance。这削弱了 Claim 3 的独立贡献。\n  tables:\n  - title: Full comparison on held-out val set\n    columns:\n    - method\n    - success\n    - verify_rate\n    - rel_cost\n    - success/cost\n    rows:\n    - - always-on\n      - 31%\n      - 100%\n      - '1.00'\n      - '0.31'\n    - - B-IAVR\n      - 27%\n      - 68%\n      - '0.72'\n      - '0.375'\n    - - random-p=0.5\n      - 26%\n      - 50%\n      - '0.55'\n      - '0.473'\n    - - confidence-thresh\n      - 25%\n      - 55%\n      - '0.60'\n      - '0.417'\n    - - no-verify\n      - 22%\n      - 0%\n      - '0.45'\n      - '0.489'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure: Pareto plot (x=cost, y=success). B-IAVR slightly above random/confidence\n    curve but not dramatically. Always-on is upper-right anchor.'\n  analysis: B-IAVR 在 absolute Pareto efficiency 上优于 baselines 但 margin 小。Random baseline\n    意外 competitive，说明 'when to verify' 的 learned signal 价值有限 at this performance level。Paper\n    需要 downplay Claim 3 到 'preliminary evidence that learned selective policy outperforms\n    naive baselines' level。可能需要 Plan B（更强 base agent）才能让 selective verification story\n    有说服力。\n- name: No-verify ablation\n  plan_id: plan_009\n  description: Episode-level GRPO without self-verification, lower bound\n  expected_results:\n    success_rate: 0.22\n    action_is_valid: 0.58\n    vs_always_on_delta: -9\n    avg_episode_length: 18\n  result_rationale: No-verify 比 always-on 低 9pp（median 档 expectation）。Verification\n    的主要价值在于 error recovery——检测并修正 invalid/ineffective actions。在 30% success 的 agent\n    中，roughly 1/3 的 success 来自 verification-triggered correction（30% × 0.3 ≈ 9pp contribution）。但\n    delta 只有 9pp 而非更大，因为：(1) 72% verification 是 confirmatory（不改变行为），(2) 部分 action\n    change 是 noise 而非 correction，(3) 一些任务不需要 verification 就能完成（simple pick tasks）。这验证了\n    verification 有 value 但也说明 always-on 的 inefficiency（72% 浪费）。\n  tables: []\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: 9pp delta 证明 verification 有 non-trivial value，支撑了 selective verification\n    的 motivation。但 delta 不够大（<10pp），使 cost-saving story 的 potential 有限——即使完美 selective，最多能恢复\n    9pp 中的大部分。\n- name: Entropy-controlled action-change analysis\n  plan_id: plan_010\n  description: Partial correlation of action-change with success after controlling\n    for policy entropy\n  expected_results:\n    raw_correlation: 0.15\n    partial_correlation_entropy_controlled: 0.11\n    p_value: 0.038\n    high_entropy_stratum_correlation: 0.08\n    low_entropy_stratum_correlation: 0.14\n    medium_entropy_stratum_correlation: 0.12\n  result_rationale: Median 档定义 action-change partial correlation 0.10-0.20，取 0.11\n    after controlling entropy。Raw correlation 从 0.15 降到 0.11（entropy 解释了部分 variance，说明\n    high-entropy states 确实倾向于产生 action change 而非 informed correction）。P-value 0.038\n    刚过 significance threshold 但不 compelling（reviewer 可能要求 Bonferroni correction 后不再\n    significant）。Low-entropy stratum correlation 更高（0.14）说明在 confident states 中 action\n    change 更可能是 informative signal，而 high-entropy 中更可能是 noise。这是 partial defense 但不是\n    strong evidence。\n  tables:\n  - title: Stratified correlation analysis\n    columns:\n    - entropy_stratum\n    - n\n    - action_change_rate\n    - correlation\n    - p_value\n    rows:\n    - - low (<0.1)\n      - '180'\n      - 18%\n      - '0.14'\n      - '0.06'\n    - - medium (0.1-0.3)\n      - '250'\n      - 28%\n      - '0.12'\n      - '0.05'\n    - - high (>0.3)\n      - '120'\n      - 42%\n      - '0.08'\n      - '0.38'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure: Three scatter plots (one per entropy stratum) showing action-change vs\n    episode success. Regression lines with CI bands.'\n  analysis: 'Signal exists but is weak and barely significant. Defense against ''action\n    change = noise'' is partial: can say ''signal persists after entropy control''\n    but effect size is small. Honest paper would acknowledge this as limitation and\n    position action-change as ''best available proxy'' rather than ''validated signal''.'\n- name: 'Causal intervention: random vs verification-triggered changes'\n  plan_id: plan_011\n  description: Inject random action changes vs verification-triggered, compare success\n  expected_results:\n    verification_triggered_success: 0.32\n    random_triggered_success: 0.24\n    no_change_baseline_success: 0.28\n    delta_triggered_vs_random: 8\n    delta_triggered_vs_nochange: 4\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档下 verification-triggered changes 比 random changes 好 8pp。原因：verification\n    过程给 model 额外 context（重新审视 state），使得 change 更 informed。但 delta 只有 8pp 而非 15+pp（strong\n    档），因为：(1) 30% success agent 的 verification quality 中等（不是所有 verification-triggered\n    change 都是 correct），(2) random change 有时碰巧也有用（ALFWorld action space 有限，random valid\n    action 有 non-trivial hit rate），(3) ''no change baseline'' 成功率 28% 意味着很多 episodes\n    不需要 correction 就能 succeed/fail。Interesting finding: triggered > no-change > random?\n    No — triggered > no-change, random < no-change. Random changes 实际上 hurt（从 28%\n    → 24%），verification-triggered 才是 helpful。'\n  tables:\n  - title: Causal intervention results\n    columns:\n    - condition\n    - success_rate\n    - n_episodes\n    - vs_baseline\n    rows:\n    - - verification-triggered change\n      - 32%\n      - '200'\n      - +4pp\n    - - no change (baseline)\n      - 28%\n      - '200'\n      - —\n    - - random change (same rate)\n      - 24%\n      - '200'\n      - -4pp\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure: Bar chart with confidence intervals. Verification-triggered > baseline\n    > random. Stars for significance.'\n  analysis: Provides causal evidence that verification adds value (not just noise).\n    But effect size moderate (+4pp vs baseline, +8pp vs random). Combined with entropy\n    analysis, forms a 'converging evidence' argument for action-change being a real\n    signal, even if weak individually.\n- name: Reward signal ablation\n  plan_id: plan_012\n  description: B-IAVR with action-change vs random-trigger vs confidence-based reward\n  expected_results:\n    action_change_success: 0.27\n    action_change_verify_rate: 0.68\n    random_trigger_success: 0.25\n    random_trigger_verify_rate: 0.62\n    confidence_reward_success: 0.24\n    confidence_verify_rate: 0.7\n  result_rationale: Median 档下 action-change reward 优于 alternatives 但 margin 小。Action-change\n    (27%, verify 68%) vs random-trigger (25%, verify 62%) delta = 2pp success, +6pp\n    verify rate。原因：(1) random trigger reward 无 informative signal，模型学到的 verify 策略接近\n    uniform random，(2) confidence-based reward 在 1.7B model 上不好估计（model 的 logit calibration\n    差，confidence 不 correlate well with actual uncertainty），(3) action-change 虽然 noisy\n    但至少有 partial signal（r=0.11）。Margin 小因为 base signal 本身弱——在 strong 档下差异会更明显。\n  tables:\n  - title: Reward signal comparison\n    columns:\n    - reward_type\n    - success\n    - verify_rate\n    - cost_reduction\n    - training_stability\n    rows:\n    - - action-change (ours)\n      - 27%\n      - 68%\n      - 28%\n      - moderate (converges step 40)\n    - - random trigger\n      - 25%\n      - 62%\n      - 35%\n      - unstable (high variance)\n    - - confidence-based\n      - 24%\n      - 70%\n      - 26%\n      - slow convergence\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: Action-change is best but advantage is modest (2-3pp). Paper can claim\n    'action-change outperforms baselines' but the weak margin means a reviewer could\n    argue the differences are within noise. Need to frame carefully with error bars\n    and multiple seeds.\n- name: ARES reproduction + comparison\n  plan_id: plan_013\n  description: Reproduce ARES SFT router on ALFWorld, head-to-head with B-IAVR\n  expected_results:\n    ares_success: 0.26\n    ares_verify_rate: 0.58\n    ares_cost_reduction: 0.38\n    biavr_success: 0.27\n    biavr_verify_rate: 0.68\n    biavr_cost_reduction: 0.28\n    delta_success: 1\n    delta_cost: -10\n  result_rationale: ARES 使用 SFT router（从 oracle labels 学 when to verify），在 cost reduction\n    上优于 B-IAVR（38% vs 28%）但 success 相近（26% vs 27%）。原因：(1) SFT 有 direct supervision\n    signal（teacher-labeled 'should verify here'），训练更 clean，(2) 但 SFT labels 是 frozen（从一个\n    checkpoint 生成），不 adapt to policy improvement，所以 success 不如 RL-trained 的 B-IAVR，(3)\n    ARES 的 continuous effort allocation 在 ALFWorld binary 场景中退化为 threshold，效果有限。Head-to-head\n    中 B-IAVR 不 clearly dominate ARES — 不同 trade-off point。这削弱了 'B-IAVR dominates'\n    的 claim。\n  tables:\n  - title: ARES vs B-IAVR head-to-head\n    columns:\n    - method\n    - success\n    - verify_rate\n    - cost_reduction\n    - training_data_needed\n    rows:\n    - - ARES (SFT router)\n      - 26%\n      - 58%\n      - 38%\n      - oracle labels required\n    - - B-IAVR (RL)\n      - 27%\n      - 68%\n      - 28%\n      - no labels (self-supervised)\n    - - always-on\n      - 31%\n      - 100%\n      - 0%\n      - —\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure: Pareto plot with ARES and B-IAVR as labeled points. Neither dominates\n    the other — ARES better on cost, B-IAVR better on success.'\n  analysis: ARES comparison doesn't favor our method on cost reduction. Differentiation\n    must come from methodology (no oracle labels needed, RL-based adaptation) rather\n    than performance numbers. Paper should frame as 'comparable performance without\n    supervision' rather than 'superior performance'.\n- name: ScienceWorld transfer\n  plan_id: plan_014\n  description: Episode-level vs step-independent on ScienceWorld environment\n  expected_results:\n    episode_level_success: 0.18\n    step_independent_success: 0.04\n    improvement_ratio: 4.5\n    episode_level_std: 0.05\n    convergence_slower: true\n    steps_to_plateau: 25\n  result_rationale: Median 档下 transfer 到 ScienceWorld 仍显示 episode-level 优势（4.5x）但\n    absolute performance 较低（18% vs ALFWorld 的 30%）。原因：(1) ScienceWorld 比 ALFWorld\n    更复杂（更长 episode、更大 action space、partial observability），(2) 1.7B 模型在 science reasoning\n    上能力有限，(3) step-independent 在更长 horizon（ScienceWorld 40-50 步）下崩溃更严重（4% vs ALFWorld\n    的 3%），(4) 收敛更慢因为 reward 更 sparse。Results 支持 generalization claim 但 18% absolute\n    performance 不算 impressive。\n  tables:\n  - title: ScienceWorld transfer results\n    columns:\n    - method\n    - success_rate\n    - improvement_vs_step_ind\n    rows:\n    - - step-independent (h=2)\n      - 4%\n      - baseline\n    - - step-independent (h=10)\n      - 9%\n      - 2.3x\n    - - episode-level GRPO\n      - 18%\n      - 4.5x\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure: Learning curves for episode-level vs step-independent on ScienceWorld.\n    Slower convergence but same qualitative pattern as ALFWorld.'\n  analysis: 'Supports generalization: dual mechanism failure is not ALFWorld-specific.\n    But low absolute numbers (18%) limit the impact claim. Paper can use this as ''consistent\n    across environments'' evidence for Claim 1 diagnostic.'\n- name: 7B model scaling verification\n  plan_id: plan_015\n  description: Episode-level vs step-independent on Qwen3-7B\n  expected_results:\n    episode_7b_success: 0.42\n    step_ind_7b_success: 0.08\n    improvement_ratio: 5.25\n    episode_7b_vs_1.7b_delta: 10\n    step_ind_7b_vs_1.7b_delta: 5\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档下 7B 模型 episode-level 达到 42%（vs 1.7B 的 32%），step-independent\n    仍 collapse 到 8%（vs 1.7B 的 3%，7B 有更好 base capabilities 所以 collapse 后仍保留一些）。Episode-level\n    的 10pp 提升来自 larger model 的 better base reasoning/planning。Step-independent 的 slight\n    improvement（8% vs 3%）因为 7B 在短 window 内也能做更好的 local decisions，但 sign misattribution\n    仍然阻止真正的 improvement。Key finding: scaling 不能 fix step-independent 的 structural\n    problem（8% 仍远低于 episode-level 的 42%）。'\n  tables:\n  - title: Model size scaling\n    columns:\n    - model\n    - episode-level\n    - step-ind (h=2)\n    - ratio\n    rows:\n    - - Qwen3-1.7B\n      - 32%\n      - 3%\n      - 10.7x\n    - - Qwen3-7B\n      - 42%\n      - 8%\n      - 5.3x\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure: 2x2 comparison (model size × training method). Episode-level scales well;\n    step-independent remains broken regardless of size.'\n  analysis: 'Supports Claim 1: step-independent failure is structural, not a model\n    capacity issue. 7B cannot compensate for broken credit assignment. Episode-level\n    benefits from scale as expected. Ratio decreases (10.7x→5.3x) but absolute gap\n    increases (29pp→34pp).'\n- name: Per-task-type breakdown\n  plan_id: plan_016\n  description: ALFWorld success breakdown by task type for episode-level\n  expected_results:\n    put_success: 0.4\n    clean_success: 0.32\n    heat_success: 0.28\n    cool_success: 0.3\n    examine_success: 0.18\n    pick_two_success: 0.15\n    correlation_with_length: -0.72\n    short_task_advantage: 12\n  result_rationale: 'Median 档下 per-task 差异明显：simple tasks（put: 40%）远好于 complex tasks（examine:\n    18%, pick_two: 15%）。原因：(1) 短 episode tasks（put 通常 10-15 步）在 episode-level 下 credit\n    assignment 更 focused（fewer actions dilute the signal），(2) Complex tasks 需要 multi-step\n    planning（先找 object、再找 tool、再执行），30% overall success 的 agent 在需要 3+ correct decisions\n    的 task 上 success 急剧下降，(3) pick_two 需要 remember 两个 target objects——working memory\n    challenge for 1.7B。Length-success correlation -0.72 confirms episode complexity\n    is key difficulty factor。'\n  tables:\n  - title: Per-task breakdown (episode-level, step 15)\n    columns:\n    - task_type\n    - success\n    - avg_steps\n    - action_is_valid\n    - n_val\n    rows:\n    - - put\n      - 40%\n      - '12.3'\n      - 62%\n      - '10'\n    - - clean\n      - 32%\n      - '18.7'\n      - 55%\n      - '6'\n    - - cool\n      - 30%\n      - '16.2'\n      - 58%\n      - '4'\n    - - heat\n      - 28%\n      - '17.8'\n      - 53%\n      - '4'\n    - - examine\n      - 18%\n      - '24.5'\n      - 48%\n      - '3'\n    - - pick_two\n      - 15%\n      - '28.1'\n      - 45%\n      - '5'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Figure: Scatter plot of task avg_steps vs success_rate with fitted regression\n    line. Clear negative correlation (-0.72).'\n  analysis: 'Confirms intuition: episode-level advantage is largest for simpler tasks\n    where credit can be assigned more cleanly. Complex tasks remain challenging even\n    with episode-level training — potential direction for future work (hierarchical\n    RL or subgoal decomposition). Useful for paper''s ''limitation'' section.'\n","numLines":833,"startLine":1,"totalLines":833}}}
